@* Orientation is the whole of it. Every vertical rule in this family is written
   group-data-[orientation=vertical]/tabs — the column layout, the full-width triggers, the
   indicator moving from the bottom edge to the trailing one — so setting layout classes by hand
   instead left the component in its horizontal state wearing a row of overrides.

   The compiler does not care which way the list runs; it moves focus with the arrow keys either
   way. *@
<Tabs Value="general" Orientation="vertical" Class="w-[520px] gap-6">
    <TabsList>
        <TabsTrigger Value="general">General</TabsTrigger>
        <TabsTrigger Value="billing">Billing</TabsTrigger>
        <TabsTrigger Value="team">Team</TabsTrigger>
    </TabsList>
    <div class="flex-1">
        <TabsContent Value="general" Class="text-sm text-muted-foreground">Name, timezone, language.</TabsContent>
        <TabsContent Value="billing" Hidden Class="text-sm text-muted-foreground">Card ending 6411.</TabsContent>
        <TabsContent Value="team" Hidden Class="text-sm text-muted-foreground">Three people.</TabsContent>
    </div>
</Tabs>
